        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2-4x+1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2\\pm\\sqrt{3}$",
          "worked": "The coefficients are $a=1$, $b=-4$, $c=1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}b^2-4ac&=(-4)^2-4(1)(1)\\\\b^2-4ac&=12\\\\x&=\\frac{4\\pm\\sqrt{12}}{2}\\\\x&=\\frac{4\\pm2\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\x&=2\\pm\\sqrt{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y^2+3y-3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\dfrac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{21}}{2}$",
          "worked": "The coefficients are $a=1$, $b=3$, $c=-3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}b^2-4ac&=3^2-4(1)(-3)\\\\b^2-4ac&=21\\\\y&=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{21}}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$t^2+6t+4=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=-3\\pm\\sqrt{5}$",
          "worked": "The coefficients are $a=1$, $b=6$, $c=4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}b^2-4ac&=6^2-4(1)(4)\\\\b^2-4ac&=20\\\\t&=\\frac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{20}}{2}\\\\t&=\\frac{-6\\pm2\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\\\t&=-3\\pm\\sqrt{5}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$3x^2-2x-2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{1\\pm\\sqrt{7}}{3}$",
          "worked": "The coefficients are $a=3$, $b=-2$, $c=-2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}b^2-4ac&=(-2)^2-4(3)(-2)\\\\b^2-4ac&=28\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{28}}{6}\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm2\\sqrt{7}}{6}\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt{7}}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q7-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$2a^2+5a-5=0$",
